    "Apply and audit Osterwalder--Schrader reconstruction for gauge-invariant continuum Yang--Mills data and derive the exact Hamiltonian spectral conclusion from positive Euclidean correlations. Use when a continuum Euclidean construction must become a physical Hilbert space with vacuum, positive energy, and a mass gap.",
    "---\nname: ym-reconstruct-os-gap\ndescription: Apply and audit Osterwalder--Schrader reconstruction for gauge-invariant continuum Yang--Mills data and derive the exact Hamiltonian spectral conclusion from positive Euclidean correlations. Use when a continuum Euclidean construction must become a physical Hilbert space with vacuum, positive energy, and a mass gap.\n---\n\n## Abducer Integration Guards\n\n- Activate this skill only for `yang-mills-existence-and-mass-gap-target` or an explicitly marked Yang-Mills calibration task.\n- Treat imported representational-dynamics artifacts as restricted, finite, conditional, or support evidence unless a later proof discharges their frontier hypotheses.\n- Emit claim level, non-claims, hard gate, hypotheses, falsifier, and demotion trigger before any promotion.\n- Compose with the target-neutral proof-depth skills: pressure formalization, hard-gate selection, nontriviality audit, anti-definitionality audit, same-domain transfer certification, and declarative learning extraction.\n- State efficient representation requirements: preserved observables, morphisms or recovery maps, invariants, error budgets, equivalence policy, locality or cutoff budget, transfer interface, and falsifiers.\n- Do not let a transfer theorem pass if the target property is built into the bridge definition; require independently stated source and target objects plus a consequence delta.\n- Preserve the four-cycle, recursion-depth-one publication-consolidation limit for local subgoals.\n- Source provenance: `agentic/external/yang_mills_representational_dynamics/2026-07-20/skill_bundle/11_vscode_codex_skill_bundle/.agents/skills/ym-reconstruct-os-gap/SKILL.md`.\n\n## Mathematical Invariants\n\nPreserve the Yang--Mills mathematical object: compact simple gauge group, pure gauge content, gauge-invariant observable algebra, regulator/cutoff/volume/coupling regime, reflection positivity, locality, OS reconstruction route, continuum limit order, and Hamiltonian spectral target. Any representation, morphism, RG step, or restricted model must state which invariants are preserved, which error budgets are allowed, and which edge case or counterexample would break transfer.\n\n## Epistemic Discipline\n\nEvery output must state epistemic status, claim level, evidence citation, source artifacts, explicit unknowns, and validation handoff. Treat physical relevance, literature-gap warrant, and frontier comparison as hard gates; unsupported implications stay conditional, blocked, or `requires_prior_art`.\n\n## Failure/Demotion\n\nDemote or quarantine if the skill assumes a mass gap, clustering, confinement, continuum existence, regulator independence, positivity, locality, observable density, or theory identity instead of proving it. Disconfirming evidence, prior-art collision, target-equivalent bridge definitions, or missing counterexample tests block promotion to a major YM publication pathway.\n\n# Reconstruct OS Gap\n\n## Objective\n\nRecover the physical Hilbert space, vacuum, Euclidean time semigroup, Hamiltonian, and spectrum, then translate uniform temporal rigidity into a gap above the vacuum.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Verify the precise OS axioms and regularity assumptions for the declared gauge-invariant Schwinger functions.\n2. Form the positive-time pre-Hilbert space, quotient its null vectors, and complete it.\n3. Construct translations and the contraction semigroup; identify its positive self-adjoint generator `H`.\n4. Establish the vacuum vector and prove uniqueness when required.\n5. Prove that the chosen observable core is dense in the reconstructed physical space.\n6. Apply the positive spectral-measure lemma to exclude spectrum in `(0,m)` from uniform temporal correlation decay.\n7. Establish the presence of a finite-energy nonvacuum state or nonempty spectrum above the gap if the target formulation requires it.\n8. State separately any results about confinement, particle poles, isolated one-particle states, or scattering. None follows merely from a spectral gap.\n\n## Audit Points\n\n- Positivity is reflection positivity, not positivity of the Euclidean action alone.\n- Spatial clustering does not replace temporal semigroup control without an additional theorem.\n- A gap seen by an incomplete observable sector is only sectorial.\n- Vacuum degeneracy changes the spectral statement.\n- The mass gap does not by itself identify particles or prove confinement.\n\n## Output Contract\n\nReturn the reconstructed objects, axiom-to-construction dependency map, density proof status, spectral-measure argument, precise spectrum inclusion, and any nonemptiness or uniqueness assumptions. Stop at a conditional OS-gap theorem if an axiom, density statement, or continuum estimate is missing.\n\n## Packaged PRISM Output Contract\n\nReturn exactly the generated `ConditionalDerivationPacket` JSON object. Do not paraphrase closed variant values.\n\n- Follow the exact generated JSON schema without extra fields.\n",
    "{\"agents/openai.yaml\":\"\"}",
)
